Here are the **Specifications, Technology Stack, and Project Structure** of the **AI Trip Planner** project:

---

### 📋 1. Project Specifications
* **Core Goal**: A full-stack web application that automatically curates day-by-day travel itineraries based on destination, duration, budget, travel style, and interests using AI.
* **Mapping and Navigation**: Leverages free, open-source mapping services instead of expensive proprietary APIs (like Google Maps) to keep core operations 100% free.
* **Security & Auth**: Includes secure dual-token JWT authentication:
  * **Access Token**: Short-lived (15 minutes), sent in API headers.
  * **Refresh Token**: Long-lived (7 days), stored securely in HTTP-only cookies.
  * **Safety Checks**: Includes rate-limiting on sensitive routes, Helmet security headers, password hashing (bcrypt), and input sanitization (MongoDB anti-injection).

---

### 💻 2. Technology Stack

| Tier | Technology | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Frontend** | **React 18** | High-performance user interface architecture |
| | **React Router v6** | Client-side page navigation |
| | **Tailwind CSS** | Premium responsive layout and styling |
| | **Framer Motion** | Micro-interactive page transitions and animations |
| | **React Query (TanStack)** | API request state caching and management |
| | **React Leaflet** | Renders maps using OpenStreetMap tiles |
| **Backend** | **Node.js & Express** | Lightweight REST API endpoint router |
| | **MongoDB & Mongoose** | NoSQL database storage and database ODM modeling |
| | **Socket.IO** | Real-time user notification events |
| | **Winston** | Structured system logs |
| **External Services** | **Google Gemini AI** | Primary AI engine for itinerary compilation |
| | **Groq API** | High-speed backup LLM server |
| | **Nominatim** | Free geocoding and coordinates lookup |
| | **OSRM** | Free OSRM turn-by-turn routing engine |

